  "description": "CUVMEN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H78 Fe4 N12 O42 Y2,3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.171-3.875 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.61-110.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe4IIIY2III(μ3-OH)2(mdea)4(m-NO2C6H4COO)8]·3MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
